#
## Copy to .env and fill in only the providers you use. Never commit real keys.
##
##   cp .env.example .env && $EDITOR .env
##   docker compose up -d
##
## Every key is optional EXCEPT AGENTGATEWAY_API_KEY. An unset key leaves that
## one provider returning 401 while the rest of the gateway still starts.
##
## Why every line below is written as a bare `NAME=`:
## agentgateway shell-expands its whole config file at load time, and an
## *undefined* variable is a hard startup error while an *empty* one is fine.
## docker-compose.yml therefore passes each name through as `${NAME:-}`, so a
## name left unset on the host arrives in the container as an empty string.
##
## The same rule applies to comments: expansion runs over the WHOLE file,
## comments included. Never spell out a dollar-sign variable reference for a
## name that is not actually set — doing so is what once broke `--validate-only`.
##

## The key clients send to the gateway (llm.policies.apiKey, mode: strict).
## REQUIRED — it deliberately has no default, so compose refuses to start
## without it rather than registering an empty key that strict mode accepts.
## Generate one, e.g. `openssl rand -hex 24`.
AGENTGATEWAY_API_KEY=agw_sk_CHANGE_ME_SECRET

## Where the UI saves config edits. file = the UI rewrites config.yaml (the
## config mount must stay writable); hybrid = config.yaml is a baseline and UI
## edits go to the database; readOnly = the UI cannot change config.
AGENTGATEWAY_STORAGE_MODE=file

## --- Provider keys --------------------------------------------------------
## The gateway routes each model prefix to one provider: anthropic/*, openai/*,
## gemini/*, mistral/*, openrouter/*, xai/*, ollama/*, ollama1|2|3/*, opencode/*.
## Leave a key blank to disable just that route.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
OPENAI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY=
MISTRAL_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
XAI_API_KEY=
OPENCODE_API_KEY=

## Gemini goes through Google's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, because the native
## one rejects an AI Studio API key sent as a Bearer token. Override only to
## point at a proxy.
GEMINI_BASE_URL=https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/openai

## --- Ollama ---------------------------------------------------------------
## Three Ollama Cloud accounts, one key each. The ollama-deepseek-balanced
## virtual model spreads DeepSeek traffic across all three; ollama1/*, ollama2/*
## and ollama3/* address one account directly.
OLLAMA_API_KEY_1=
OLLAMA_API_KEY_2=
OLLAMA_API_KEY_3=

## Local Ollama needs no key. Inside a container localhost is the container
## itself, so docker-compose.yml overrides this to host.docker.internal.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:11434/v1

## --- Other providers ------------------------------------------------------
## Ollama Cloud (https://ollama.com/v1) is reached through the ollama1..3 keys
## above; this block covers the local prismml endpoint and OpenCode's Zen API.
## prismml defaults to a local-only key, so it needs no real secret.
OPENCODE_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/go/v1
PRISMML_BASE_URL=http://host.docker.internal:8477/v1
PRISMML_API_KEY=local

## --- MCP ------------------------------------------------------------------
## Tavily's remote MCP server takes its key in the URL query, not a header.
TAVILY_API_KEY=

## --- Storage --------------------------------------------------------------
## Request log, usage and cost history. docker-compose.yml overrides this to
## reach the Postgres sibling service; the value here is the localhost default,
## used only when running the gateway binary directly with ./run.sh.
AGENTGATEWAY_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://agentgateway:agentgateway@localhost:5432/agentgateway
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=agentgateway

## Cost catalogs, resolved against the working directory inside the container.
AGENTGATEWAY_BASE_COSTS=./base-costs.json
AGENTGATEWAY_PI_ALIASES=./pi-aliases.json

## --- Jaeger ----------------------------------------------------------------
## Host port for the Jaeger UI (http://127.0.0.1:16686). Change it if something
## already holds 16686 — Jaeger Desktop does — otherwise compose fails with
## "Bind for 0.0.0.0:16686 failed: port is already allocated".
# JAEGER_UI_PORT=16686

## --- Azure (not configured) -----------------------------------------------
## docker-compose.yml passes these three through, but config.yaml defines no
## azure provider, so nothing reads them. The gateway refuses to start without
## a resource name, so add the provider and an azure/* model to config.yaml
## first, then set these.
# AZUREOPENAI_API_KEY=
# AZURE_OPENAI_RESOURCE_NAME=
# AZURE_OPENAI_API_VERSION=2024-10-21
